  "result": "I fixed all three problems in `src/queue.js`, and `npm test` passes with 6 of 6 tests green. I didn't run the new tests against the old code, so I haven't confirmed they fail without the fix.\n\n- **Hang after a failure:** a rejected job never decremented `running`. A job that threw synchronously, or returned a plain value instead of a promise, also broke the queue. Every job's outcome now goes through one path that always frees its slot and starts the next job. That covers rejections, sync throws and plain return values.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving early:** it only checked that nothing was pending. It now also waits for `running` to reach 0.\n- **Only one job after `resume()`:** `next()` started a single job per call. It now loops until every free slot is filled or the queue is empty or paused.\n\nI added four regression tests in `test/queue.test.js`:\n- the queue keeps going after an async rejection, a sync throw and a plain return value;\n- `onIdle()` waits for jobs that are already running;\n- `onIdle()` resolves immediately when the queue is idle;\n- after `pause()` and `resume()` with concurrency 4, four jobs run at once.",
